<h2>Security defaults</h2>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Default</th><th>What it prevents</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>storeAuthRequests: false</code></td><td>Storing requests with auth headers; prevents replaying expired credentials</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>storeNonIdempotent: false</code></td><td>Storing POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE without idempotency key; prevents duplicate side effects</td></tr>
    <tr><td>No <code>rehydrateAuth</code> by default</td><td>Replayed requests carry no auth unless you explicitly provide fresh tokens</td></tr>
